I. Definitions
A. (n;n_1,n_2,\cdot\cdot\cdot\cdot,n_n_\infty) is the number of ways of putting n=n_1+n_2+\cdot\cdot\cdot+n_\infty different objects into m different boxes with n_k in the k-th box, k=1, 2, \cdot\cdot\cdot, m.
(n; a_1, a_2,\cdot\cdot\cdot,a_n_\infty)* is the number of permutations of n=a_1+2a_2+\cdot\cdot\cdot+na_\infty symbols composed of a_k cycles of length k for k=1, 2, \cdot\cdot\cdot, n.
(n; a_1, a_2,\cdot\cdot\cdot,a_n_\infty)' is the number of ways of partitioning a set of n=a_1+2a_2+\cdot\cdot\cdot+na_\infty different objects into a_k subsets containing k objects for k=1, 2, \cdot\cdot\cdot, n.
